 narrowed since 2020"], "rationale": "With no polls, ratings, or market pricing for this race, the forecast rests on New York's partisan lean, which has favored Democrats by high single digits in recent presidential elections even as the margin narrowed in 2024.", "watch": "The first credible state polls or a sharp shift in the national environment could move the margin meaningfully in either direction.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "New York remains a Democratic-leaning state in presidential politics, though its margin has narrowed over recent cycles. With the incumbent president term-limited, both parties will nominate new standard-bearers, and no candidate-specific polling or expert ratings are yet available for the general election. The forecast therefore rests on the state's underlying partisan lean of roughly eight points.\n\nHeadlines so far focus on the Democratic primary field, where early surveys show a contested nomination, but these say little about the general election in New York itself. The state's presidential margins have drifted toward Republicans since 2020, which keeps meaningful uncertainty in the estimate. As things stand, the Democratic nominee holds a clear but not overwhelming edge, and the race would likely become genuinely competitive only if the national environment shifted sharply.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8251, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7779, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.769, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7679, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7809, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7813, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7727, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-